WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.365 --> 00:00:01.865
ALEXIS MOUSSINE-POUCHKINE:
So you're

00:00:01.865 --> 00:00:03.130
new to Google Cloud Platform.

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:06.250
Maybe you would like to simply
check out GCP's breadth,

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:08.170
deploy some
application of yours,

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:11.410
or learn about Google Cloud's
big data and machine learning

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:12.730
capabilities.

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:14.410
In any case, welcome.

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:15.400
Let me show you around.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.872
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:24.466
So first things first,
cloud.google.com

00:00:24.466 --> 00:00:26.239
is your starting point.

00:00:26.239 --> 00:00:28.030
This is where you will
find all the product

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:32.320
information and documentation,
but also detailed solutions

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:37.120
with architectures and code
with many different use cases.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.840
Pricing is also detailed there,
including Google's pricing

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:45.010
principles and a detailed
cost calculator for every GCP

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:46.810
product and service.

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:50.920
Cloud.google.com is also
the place to access support,

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:53.950
to read customer stories,
to find partners,

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:55.630
and to understand
how Google Cloud

00:00:55.630 --> 00:00:59.170
Platform is different
from other public clouds.

00:00:59.170 --> 00:01:01.990
The Google Cloud Console
is where you will likely

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:04.569
spend a fair amount of
time exploring and using

00:01:04.569 --> 00:01:05.960
the platform.

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:08.350
This is where you configure
building accounts,

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:12.220
create and manage projects,
and manage all your GCP

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:16.780
resources, regardless of
their data center location.

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:19.600
Every product and every
service has its own section

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.890
in the console left-hand
menu, with dashboards,

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:26.020
detailed configurations,
and settings.

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:28.960
You will also find interactive
quick start experiences

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:31.540
from right inside the console.

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:34.600
Take this example quick
start for Compute Engine.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:37.750
Simply walk through the
various steps of the tutorial,

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:41.260
and within minutes, you'll be
running a Node.js application

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:45.520
with its back end on Compute
Engine virtual machines.

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:49.210
The Cloud Console also
offers a marketplace

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:53.290
with ready-to-go software stacks
to accelerate development,

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:55.120
so you spend less
time installing

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:57.160
and more time developing.

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:00.280
This allows you to deploy
production-grade solutions

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:02.950
in a few clicks with
a single bill for all

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:06.700
your GCP and third-party
costs, and it also

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:09.550
offers direct access
to partner support.

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:11.890
To make sure you set
up your employees up

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:15.390
with the right permissions to
use different GCP resources,

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:19.450
Cloud Console also integrates
Identity and Access Management,

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:23.770
or Cloud IAM, and
provides a unified view

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:28.270
into security policy across
your entire organization.

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:31.330
This is also where you
would manage quotas

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:32.800
across the platform.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:36.160
Every product comes with
one or more usage limits

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:39.430
across the platform, so
you can prevent one team

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:41.530
from spending the entire
[INAUDIBLE] budget

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:44.590
on a rote query or compute job.

00:02:44.590 --> 00:02:48.970
If you'd like, you may even use
our iOS and Android mobile apps

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:53.680
to monitor and manage your
GCP applications on the go.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:57.160
Finally, one can sign up
for affordable support

00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:00.400
for both development and
production phases right

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.530
from the console.

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:04.960
This role-based support
enables configuration

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:07.810
on a per-user basis,
and case management

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:10.630
is integrated into
Cloud Console.

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:13.580
While the console is
powerful and flexible,

00:03:13.580 --> 00:03:16.180
you can do everything
from the command line.

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:20.260
For every action in the console,
there is a gcloud equivalent.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:23.620
gcloud is our scriptable
and almighty CLI,

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:27.120
and it comes with
the Google Cloud SDK.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:29.110
Cloud Shell is a
shell environment

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:32.890
hosted on Google Cloud Platform
for managing your projects

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:34.150
and resources.

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:36.550
It is accessible from
a simple web browser

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:39.100
and is powered by a
small virtual machine

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:42.220
with persistent disk
and up-to-date software

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:44.440
for all your development needs.

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:47.290
It even comes with
a web code editor.

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:49.990
If you'd like to know more
about developer tools,

00:03:49.990 --> 00:03:54.130
check out the video linked
in the description below.

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:56.860
Before you can use
GCP Cloud Console,

00:03:56.860 --> 00:03:59.090
you will need a Google account.

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:01.270
You can create a
new Google account

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:04.990
or use an existing one,
such as your Gmail account.

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:08.360
We recommend that you enable
billing for your project,

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:10.600
and that you sign up
for our free trial.

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:12.550
If you do not
enable billing, you

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:14.530
will not be able
to use GCP products

00:04:14.530 --> 00:04:16.810
beyond their free tier.

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:18.950
If you do not sign up
for the free trial,

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:21.279
or if you're not
eligible, you can still

00:04:21.279 --> 00:04:26.080
benefit from that GCP
generous always free tier.

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:29.110
You will find more details about
the free tier and free trial

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:31.120
in an upcoming video.

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:33.310
Once logged into
the GCP Console,

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:35.890
I would recommend that you
check out the main menu,

00:04:35.890 --> 00:04:39.940
and in particular, the
Getting Started section.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:43.480
Start with a short tour
of the platform tutorial.

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:45.790
In a few minutes, you
will get a good sense

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:49.150
of how to get the best
out of Cloud Console.

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:52.150
Next, scroll to
Interactive Tutorials,

00:04:52.150 --> 00:04:55.840
and take a short hands-on lab
for the topic of your choice

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:58.470
without leaving the console.

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:01.440
Finally, check out the
main categories product

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:03.630
GCP has to offer--

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:08.550
compute, storage,
networking, Stackdriver

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:12.690
for everything DevOps,
tools, big data,

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:14.730
and artificial intelligence.

00:05:14.730 --> 00:05:17.760
As you progress through
your discovery of GCP,

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:20.580
keep in mind those
key resources--

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:26.610
documentation, in-depth
tutorials, support, training,

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:28.450
and free code labs.

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:31.600
GCP can be
overwhelming at first.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:33.510
But with this small
guidance, we hope

00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:36.780
that you are now confident
that your best ideas can

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:38.730
come to life in the cloud.

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:41.220
We're certainly excited
to see what you build

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:43.950
and look forward
to your feedback.

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:47.430
If you like this video, please
like, subscribe, comment,

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:50.940
share, and look forward to
more GCP Essentials videos.

00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:54.290
[MUSIC PLAYING]

